WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.202 --> 00:00:04.541
- It can have a very, not
necessarily oppressive

00:00:04.541 --> 00:00:06.963
but kind of weighty presence on you.

00:00:06.963 --> 00:00:08.382
(whooshing)

00:00:08.382 --> 00:00:11.022
(creaking)

00:00:11.022 --> 00:00:13.283
- My relationship with the
word Asian can sometimes

00:00:13.283 --> 00:00:14.483
be a little complicated.

00:00:14.483 --> 00:00:16.323
- Being Asian informs most of my identity.

00:00:16.323 --> 00:00:18.902
- Sometimes I will identity as Asian,

00:00:18.902 --> 00:00:22.602
but then other Indian people
don't identify as Asian.

00:00:22.602 --> 00:00:23.544
- Why are you considered Asian,

00:00:23.544 --> 00:00:25.383
you're in the Pacific
Islander, wouldn't you

00:00:25.383 --> 00:00:26.662
be considered more Hawaiian?

00:00:26.662 --> 00:00:28.662
And I'm like, not really.

00:00:28.662 --> 00:00:31.244
- I have this awareness
that it's the first thing

00:00:31.244 --> 00:00:32.822
that people notice about me.

00:00:32.822 --> 00:00:35.282
- People associate Asian with East Asian.

00:00:35.282 --> 00:00:37.142
- Filipinos aren't so much dismissed,

00:00:37.142 --> 00:00:38.283
they're just overlooked just because

00:00:38.283 --> 00:00:40.994
they're not as popular within, at least

00:00:40.994 --> 00:00:41.904
the American culture.

00:00:41.904 --> 00:00:44.523
- If you think about it,
the world population,

00:00:44.523 --> 00:00:47.365
60% of it is technically Asians.

00:00:47.365 --> 00:00:51.767
And we don't speak of
any ethnic group at large

00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:53.406
on such a continental scale.

00:00:53.406 --> 00:00:55.483
- Asia as a term refers to a continent

00:00:55.483 --> 00:00:58.465
of like 40 to 50 different countries

00:00:58.465 --> 00:01:00.165
all with really, really different history,

00:01:00.165 --> 00:01:02.184
culture, language, religion.

00:01:02.184 --> 00:01:05.064
- But the term Asian has utility.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:08.425
It's just within that
there is so much diversity

00:01:08.425 --> 00:01:09.883
that needs to be acknowledged.

00:01:09.883 --> 00:01:14.484
And especially when you extent
that to Pacific Islanders.

00:01:14.484 --> 00:01:16.344
- People will say things
like, oh that's so Asian.

00:01:16.344 --> 00:01:17.444
Or why are you being so Asian?

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:19.145
Or like stop being so Asian.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.884
And I'm like, I'm just
trying to eat my lunch here,

00:01:20.884 --> 00:01:22.564
like I don't understand
why my lunch makes,

00:01:22.564 --> 00:01:24.185
like says that I'm being so Asian.

00:01:24.185 --> 00:01:25.303
- Even when I did my hair this morning,

00:01:25.303 --> 00:01:27.404
I was like, oh, every time
I put my hair in a bun,

00:01:27.404 --> 00:01:28.984
do I look too Asian?

00:01:28.984 --> 00:01:31.445
But, what does that even
mean, because I am Asian.

00:01:31.445 --> 00:01:34.104
- In high school I had to
deal a lot with the stereotype

00:01:34.104 --> 00:01:36.484
of being Asian and smart.

00:01:36.484 --> 00:01:38.904
Other people would say,
oh, you just did well

00:01:38.904 --> 00:01:39.983
because you're Asian.

00:01:39.983 --> 00:01:41.904
- Yes, I am Asian, and I'm proud of it,

00:01:41.904 --> 00:01:45.803
but my first identifying
feature should not be

00:01:45.803 --> 00:01:47.924
like, oh, that guy's Asian so therefore

00:01:47.924 --> 00:01:49.243
he's this, this, and this.

00:01:49.243 --> 00:01:50.704
- It's the way they're saying the word,

00:01:50.704 --> 00:01:53.765
and it's not the word itself.

00:01:53.765 --> 00:01:55.324
- The biggest source of pride for me

00:01:55.324 --> 00:01:57.744
is whenever I see fellow Asians

00:01:57.744 --> 00:02:00.584
and Asian-Americans
making their voices heard.

00:02:00.584 --> 00:02:04.045
- I have incorporated my love of India

00:02:04.045 --> 00:02:05.924
into the work that I do.

00:02:05.924 --> 00:02:09.305
- My mom has a signature
Filipino like lumpia egg rolls.

00:02:09.305 --> 00:02:11.184
I'd always bring them, and that was my way

00:02:11.184 --> 00:02:13.685
of kind of like, introducing
people to Filipino culture.

00:02:13.685 --> 00:02:15.005
- I think, I feel like the reason that

00:02:15.005 --> 00:02:19.723
I am always staunchly proud
of being an Pacific Islander

00:02:19.723 --> 00:02:21.844
specifically is to kind of raise awareness

00:02:21.844 --> 00:02:23.084
just on a personal level.

00:02:23.084 --> 00:02:25.524
- Your identity informs
everything that you do,

00:02:25.524 --> 00:02:26.967
and that's something to be celebrated,

00:02:26.967 --> 00:02:28.225
and it something to be excited about.

00:02:28.225 --> 00:02:30.024
- No matter what, you're able to identify

00:02:30.024 --> 00:02:32.905
as Asian, and you're able to
understand someone's journey.

00:02:32.905 --> 00:02:35.465
- If were able to see
Asian and Asian-American

00:02:35.465 --> 00:02:38.364
as like a group, and as a conversation,

00:02:38.364 --> 00:02:39.705
we can use something like that

00:02:39.705 --> 00:02:42.455
as a way to collectively rise up.

00:02:50.323 --> 00:02:51.526
(whooshing)

00:02:51.526 --> 00:02:52.953
(creaking)

